WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.620
Sabrina Spellman has cast her spooky spell
over Netflix in a dark, twisted new tale.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.559
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm talking all about the Chilling

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:15.260
Adventures of Sabrina, what the Season 1 ending
really means, some crucial details you might

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.369
have missed in the finale, and my season 2
theories.

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:22.800
Keep watching till the end where I'll explain
why we might see feline Salem actually speak

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
next season.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.270
Spoilers ahead, so take care if you're not
all caught up or if you prefer tap here to

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.390
watch my spoiler-free review.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:36.190
All season Sabrina resists pledging her allegiance
to the Dark Lord, but when Miss Wardwell resurrects

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.050
the Greendale 13 who in turn summon the Red
Angel of Death, Sabrina is pressured into

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.550
signing her name in the Book of the Beast.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.180
Doing this moves Sabrina's powers to a new
level, allowing her to summon forth hellfire

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.850
which burns the souls of the reanimated witches.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.800
Now, there's an interesting detail here which
you'll need to look carefully at because the

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.860
scene is quite dark, but as Sabrina completes
her transformation into a full witch, you

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.850
can see white streaks taking over her hair.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.360
We can appreciate that more fully in the final
shot of the episode and it's actually a nice

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.710
nod to Sabrina's white hair in the comics.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.840
Sabrina's definitely embraced her darker nature,
strutting along and seemingly leading the

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.520
Weird Sisters now, and you can see Nicholas
Scratch's rather concerned reaction when he

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.560
sees this, which is understandable when you
consider the sisters' nefarious deeds this

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.560
season.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.560
Also revealed in the finale is why Miss Wardwell,
aka Lilith or Madame Satan, worked so hard

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.150
to manipulate Sabrina into signing her name
in the Book of the Beast.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:38.710
By securing Sabrina's allegiance, Madame Satan
believes she'll soon reign as Queen of Hell

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.680
as a reward.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.369
Her familiar Stolas, however, points out that
it seems more likely that Satan's true plan

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:47.850
is to groom Sabrina to sit on the throne by
his side.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.689
Madame Satan's clearly displeased with this
idea and snaps the crow's neck, indicating

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:56.639
that, if that does happen, she'll deal with
Sabrina in a similar fashion.

00:01:56.639 --> 00:02:00.620
If we go back over the season there's plenty
of clues that suggest the Dark Lord has a

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.899
more particular interest in Sabrina than Lilith
might like to think.

00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:09.030
Consider how powerful Sabrina became after
signing her name in the book.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.960
When she summoned hellfire against the Greendale
13, she became only the fourth witch in history

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.379
to ever achieve that.

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:20.340
There seems to be something about Sabrina
that makes her of special interest to Satan.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.379
Remember that the marriage of Edward Spellman
to the mortal Diana was approved via a special

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:29.860
dispensation with Satan himself even blessing
the union, but Edward had to offer his child

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.129
in exchange.

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:35.360
Perhaps Satan's interested in her human half
because it could afford him some additional

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.950
power or hold over the mortal world.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.340
Let me know if you've got any theories.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.819
Madame Satan will prove no pushover though
next season as she's still got Brina fooled

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:48.989
that Miss Wardwell is just a regular witch
and I think she'll be able to continue tricking

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:52.140
Sabrina into thinking she's a helpful ally
for some time.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.290
However, something I noticed in Wardwell's
final scene is that she has the Red Angel

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.920
of Death figurine displayed prominently on
her mantelpiece.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.069
That seems to be the same figure that Ambrose
found when he discovered the Greendale 13

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:05.689
had been resurrected.

00:03:05.689 --> 00:03:10.040
And if Sabrina or Ambrose notice it next season,
they might realise there's something up with

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.030
Miss Wardwell.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.689
Another twist at the end of the season was
when we discover that Zelda has stolen away

00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:19.079
Father Blackwood's daughter to raise her together
with Hilda.

00:03:19.079 --> 00:03:23.219
Zelda lied to Blackwood about the child because
she was actually the first born and therefore

00:03:23.219 --> 00:03:24.670
his rightful heir.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:29.319
Lady Blackwood had previously told Zelda that
her husband really wanted a male heir and

00:03:29.319 --> 00:03:32.099
so Zelda feared for the baby girl's safety.

00:03:32.099 --> 00:03:36.400
It's quite possible Blackwood might deliberately
harm the new baby if he knew she was the first

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.159
born over her younger twin brother.

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:41.140
"The Church of Night is ours, boys."

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:44.170
"This is the Dark Lord's sign."

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.150
"His blessing... that we are in the right."

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:52.690
"Hail to my firstborn son."

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.569
"Hail Judas."

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:56.459
"Hail Judas!"

00:03:56.459 --> 00:04:00.920
A quick side note here, notice how horrified
Ambrose is at what's going on in this scene,

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.730
which will likely put him in conflict next
season with his boyfriend Luke, who seems

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.969
to be all on board with Blackwood's new warlock
supremacy movement.

00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:13.219
Going back to Blackwood's twin daughter, there's
another potential kink in Zelda's plan to

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:17.470
raise a girl who might challenge Blackwood's
attempt to establish an all-male hierarchy

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.340
at the Church of Night; and that is Prudence.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.910
This season Prudence discovered that she's
Blackwood's daughter but, because she was

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.940
born out of wedlock, her claim as his heir
comes second to Blackwood's children born

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.000
of his wife.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.140
However, remember what Sabrina told Pru:

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.040
"If you were Father Blackwood's daughter,
you could one day lay claim to the Church

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:42.009
of Night, this school, everything, but you'd
have to get rid of his legitimate heirs first."

00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:46.840
What if Prudence decides to hatch her own
plot to dispatch both of Blackwood's legitimate

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:47.840
children?

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:51.720
It really feels the show is setting up some
serious battles over who runs the Church of

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.690
Night next season.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:57.780
One mystery set up this season that I'm hoping
we'll get some answers to in season 2 is what

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.690
really happened with Sabrina's parents?

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:05.440
Zelda and Hilda repeatedly insist there was
no foul play involved in their death; however,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.780
the Weird Sisters dropped a big hint that
that's probably not the case:

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.830
"You don't want what happened to your mother
and father to happen to you."

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.710
"What did you say?"

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.360
"The accident... that took their lives...

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.930
It would be tragic if a similar one befell
you."

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.330
Father Blackwood definitely had issues with
Edward Spellman's ideas about reforming the

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:30.270
Church of Night and we know that Madame Satan
also resents Sabrina's parents.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.270
When the Mother of Demons takes over Miss
Wardwell's body she curses Edward and calls

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.220
Diana a "mortal sow".

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:40.990
In the Chilling Adventures of Sabrina comics,
Madame Satan and Edward Spellman were originally

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:45.180
lovers until he betrayed her in favour of
Diana, and it'll be interesting to see whether

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.960
that also becomes part of Madam Satan's backstory
in the TV show.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.050
Like Sabrina, Aunt Hilda discovers a new path
for herself by the end of the season when

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:57.970
she strikes up a relationship with bookstore
owner Dr Cerberus.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.569
With Hilda's confidence in herself growing,
she decides she wants some more autonomy from

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:05.259
her sister and announces she's moving out
of the room they share together.

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:09.680
But there's a hint that things won't play
out so smoothly, because as Dr Cerberus walks

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:14.300
away from the Spellman house, his eyes flash
for a split second, suggesting there's another

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.349
side to the bookstore owner.

00:06:16.349 --> 00:06:20.710
In Greek mythology, Cerberus was a multi-headed
dog who kept watch over the gates to the Underworld,

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:25.599
and whatever Dr Cerberus's true nature is,
it'll be interesting to see what part he plays

00:06:25.599 --> 00:06:27.370
next season.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:31.830
As for Sabrina's romantic situation, although
she clearly still loves Harvey, in the final

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.690
scene they share together she tells him that
something dark has awakened inside her so

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.950
it's not safe for her to be around him.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:42.300
This is a familiar trope we've seen many times
in film and TV, especially for superheroes,

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:46.190
for example, Spider-Man decides it's too dangerous
for him to be with Mary Jane.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:51.270
But these things never really work out and
so even if Sabrina has a fling with Nick,

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.180
her true feelings will probably remain with
Harvey.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.240
And this love triangle could be dangerous
if Nick ends up falling for Sabrina.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.949
Nick previously said he was jealous of how
mortals love each other and he seems to have

00:07:01.949 --> 00:07:04.099
a special affection for Brina.

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:08.639
A hot topic for many fans of the old-school
Sabrina sitcom is her cat Salem who, in this

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:13.669
new series, only spoke out loud briefly in
season 1, and that was in his goblin form

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:15.889
when he introduced himself as her familiar.

00:07:15.889 --> 00:07:20.690
However, when we hear Madame Satan's crow
talking to her in the finale, I think the

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:24.949
showrunners may be teasing the possibility
of a talking Salem in season 2.

00:07:24.949 --> 00:07:29.289
I don't expect we'll be getting the kind of
sassy and sarcastic wit that was so iconic

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:33.510
in Sabrina The Teenage Witch as it probably
wouldn't fit the tone of this new show.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:37.409
But I think some more Salem talking moments
would help develop his character a bit more

00:07:37.409 --> 00:07:39.539
and give us more insight into his personality.

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:44.479
There's been a lot of talk about a Riverdale
crossover with Sabrina and there were lots

00:07:44.479 --> 00:07:49.409
of references to the popular CW show in the
first season of Chilling Adventures plus a

00:07:49.409 --> 00:07:52.840
surprise cameo which I talk more about in
my other Sabrina video.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:56.159
There's a card for that here plus a link in
the video description below.

00:07:56.159 --> 00:08:00.789
I suspect that for the moment in season 2,
any crossover would be limited to a cameo

00:08:00.789 --> 00:08:05.120
again because a full-on crossover might be
tricky to pull off given the differing aesthetics

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.720
of the two shows.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:11.120
However, Sabrina or Harvey could turn up briefly
in Riverdale to set up a more substantial

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:12.669
crossover in the future.

00:08:12.669 --> 00:08:18.480
And with Riverdale seeming to go full-on supernatural
in Season 3, a cameo like this could be feasible

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:19.480
to pull off.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.520
Let me know if you've got any thoughts on
how the shows could cross over.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:25.289
Now, what were your favourite moments this
season?

00:08:25.289 --> 00:08:28.669
And do you have any theories or things you'd
like to see next on Chilling Adventures?

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:32.289
For example, do you want a talking Salem in
season 2?

